SUMMARY:Cambridge International Law Discussion Group: 'The Element of Groun
 d in Space Governance'
LOCATION:Lauterpacht Centre for International Law
URL:https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/events/cambridge-international-law-discussion
 -group-element-ground-space-governance
CATEGORIES:Law,International,Policy
DESCRIPTION:Faculty of Law\nTopics: Law\, International\, Policy\nDetails: 
 https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/events/cambridge-international-law-discussion-gr
 oup-element-ground-space-governance\nDate/time: \n\n Wednesday 18 November
  2026 \n\n 1:00pm to 2:00pm\n\n Location: \n\n Lauterpacht Centre for Inte
 rnational Law\n\n About \n\n Speaker: Yirong Sun (PhD Candidate in Law at 
 Cambridge)\n Has it ever come into your mind that satellites in outer spac
 e are deeply tied to the ground? This session will discuss the plans of a 
 two-year empirical phase (of the PhD project) using archival research\, in
 terviews and participant observation to examine how the ground concentrate
 s and redistributes power in Earth observation/remote sensing satellite mi
 ssions. Where are ground stations located\, how do particular sites become
  part of space infrastructure\, and how are land uses repurposed or intens
 ified over time? These questions bring into view actors who do not necessa
 rily own satellites themselves but whose land\, infrastructure or regulato
 ry authority helps make satellite operations possible. \n The broad
END:VEVENT
